        "raw_output": "{\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"variable\": \"structure_attitude\",\n      \"observations\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"obs_structure_attitude_1\",\n          \"stance\": \"support\",\n          \"value\": \"The user has a general preference for spontaneity and flexibility over rigid structure in their hobbies and creative work. They have abandoned writing reviews because they feel structured formats stifle creativity and limit free-flowing thought, preferring discussions that allow spontaneous and genuine expression. They lost interest in a book review blog because it became a chore and the pressure to produce content drained their enthusiasm. They tried fan fiction but felt it no longer matched their evolving personal style, seeking more authentic original writing. They tried creating art based on book themes but it did not resonate. They later resumed blogging about books, finding it a fulfilling outlet for self-expression and connection. They explicitly state a preference for casual, relaxed settings without rigid formats, emphasizing enjoyment and free-flowing ideas over structure.\",\n          \"source_ids\": [\"s3\", \"s4\", \"s13\", \"s14\", \"s15\", \"s23\", \"s24\", \"s31\", \"s32\", \"s33\", \"s41\", \"s42\", \"s43\", \"s46\", \"s47\", \"s48\"],\n          \"entity_scope\": \"user\",\n          \"time_scope\": \"past\",\n          \"parent_versions\": {},\n          \"retract_ids\": [],\n          \"reason\": \"The user's statements across multiple conversations consistently express a preference for spontaneity and flexibility over rigid structure in their hobbies (writing reviews, blogging, fan fiction, art, book discussions). They explicitly state that structured formats feel stifling and that they prefer casual, relaxed settings. The summary captures the overall pattern of their attitudes toward structure vs. spontaneity in their creative and literary pursuits.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    }\n  