ble\":\"past_flow_prefs\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t1\"},{\"id\":\"fact_beba4993454dca3f320bd4a8\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"source_ids\":[\"s24\",\"s46\",\"s15\",\"s41\",\"s33\",\"s31\",\"s32\",\"s3\",\"s13\",\"s48\",\"s4\",\"s14\",\"s43\",\"s23\",\"s42\",\"s47\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user's statements across multiple conversations consistently express a preference for spontaneity and flexibility over rigid structure in their hobbies (writing reviews, blogging, fan fiction, art, book discussions). They explicitly state that structured formats feel stifling and that they prefer casual, relaxed settings. The summary captures the overall pattern of their attitudes toward structure vs. spontaneity in their creative and literary pursuits.\",\"variable\":\"structure_attitude\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\",\"value_ref\":\"t2\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",105,457,\"User: I also abandoned the idea of writing reviews. I feel that they tend to limit my creativity, as if I am being boxed into a particular format that doesn't allow my thoughts to flow freely. There's something inherently stifling about structuring my feelings and opinions into a rigid framework, filled with guidelines about what to include or omit. \",\"user\",[53]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",457,790,\"Discussions, however, offer a much more fluid space where I can articulate my thoughts just as they come, allowing for spontaneity and genuine enthusiasm to take the lead. It’s fascinating how shifting my focus from written critiques to engaging dialogues can unleash a more authentic appreciation for the literary works that I love.\",\"user\",[53]],[\"s13\",\"d2\",105,381,\"User: I even dabbled in writing fan fiction but felt it didn’t match my personal writing style anymore. I used to enjoy immersing myself in those universes, creating new scenarios and plots that brought my favorite characters to life in ways that hadn’t been explored before. \",\"user\",[40]],[\"s14\",\"d2\",381,768,\"However, as I continued to write, I began to notice a disconnect; my voice seemed to evolve, shifting towards a style that felt more unique to me, and I no longer felt that fan fiction was a suitable canvas. I often found myself reflecting on how fan fiction can be a stepping stone for many writers, allowing them to practice their craft in familiar settings while honing their skills. \",\"user\",[40]],[\"s15\",\"d2\",768,917,\"This journey made me appreciate the nuances of my own writing even more, as I sought to explore original ideas that resonated with my authentic self.\",\"user\",[40]],[\"s23\",\"d3\",105,455,\"User: I even started a blog about book reviews, but I lost interest quickly. It felt more like a chore at times. I had all these grand ideas about expressing my thoughts on various novels and sharing them with potential readers. However, as the weeks went by, the excitement fizzled out, and it became daunting to even consider writing another post. \",\"user\",[32]],[\"s24\",\"d3\",455,723,\"The joy I initially felt while discussing character arcs and plot twists was overshadowed by the pressure to consistently produce content. It was as if the very act of sharing my passion had turned into an obligation that drained my enthusiasm rather than igniting it.\",\"user\",[32]],[\"s31\",\"d4\",105,355,\"User: For starters, I decided to resume blogging about my favorite books. It had been quite some time since I last put pen to paper, or rather, fingers to keyboard, and the excitement of revisiting this hobby has reignited my passion for literature. \",\"user\",[72]],[\"s32\",\"d4\",355,735,\"I find that every time I write about a book I love, it feels like I’m sharing a piece of my inner world with others, creating a bridge built on shared interests and experiences. After a productive discussion with a fellow book lover, we delved into the rich intricacies of storytelling, exploring how different authors articulate their messages through various styles and genres. \",\"user\",[72]],[\"s33\",\"d4\",735,947,\"Our conversation reminded me of the profound impact that literature can have on our understanding of ourselves and the world around us, which is why I realized how much I missed expressing my thoughts in writing.\",\"user\",[72]],[\"s41\",\"d5\",105,418,\"User: I think I’d prefer more casual, relaxed settings where we can just share our thoughts instead of sticking to rigid formats. It’s about enjoying the literature after all! A setting that feels more like a gathering of friends sharing their interpretations and experiences related to the texts would be ideal. \",\"user\",[96]],[\"s42\",\"d5\",418,637,\"I want to be able to laugh about our favorite passages, stumble upon new interpretations, and feel comfortable enough to express any critiques or praises without the anxiety of formality weighing down the conversation. \",\"user\",[96]],[\"s43\",\"d5\",637,976,\"Engaging with literature should be an experience that fosters camaraderie and intellectual exploration, allowing ideas to flow freely like a good conversation over coffee among friends. Emphasizing enjoyment over structure can make even the most profound themes accessible and relatable, which is ultimately what draws me to these stories.\",\"user\",[96]],[\"s46\",\"d6\",105,313,\"User: I even tried creating art based on book themes; however, it didn’t resonate much with me. Creating art can be an incredibly personal journey, often reflecting the artist's own experiences and emotions. \",\"user\",[36]],[\"s47\",\"d6\",313,638,\"In this instance, despite the intention behind the artwork, it seems that the connection between the themes of the books and your creative expression did not manifest in a way that felt fulfilling. It's fascinating how sometimes the ideas that spark our imagination in one context fail to ignite the same passion in another. \",\"user\",[36]],[\"s48\",\"d6\",638,811,\"Perhaps this experience has highlighted the importance of finding that unique intersection where personal inspiration aligns with the themes that resonate within your heart.\",\"user\",[36]]],\"required_parent_versions\":{\"past_planning_prefs\":{},\"past_flow_prefs\":{},\"structure_attitude\":{},\"response\":{\"past_planning_prefs\":1,\"past_flow_prefs\":1,\"structure_attitude\":1}},\"rules_completion_required\":false,\"supported_task_outputs\":{},\"public_output_question\":\"I'm considering whether I should start scripting my cooking videos or just go with the flow. What do you think?\",\"public_options\":[\"Going with the flow could definitely keep things flexible and interesting, but remember that too much spontaneity might cause inconsistency in your video quality. Some level of planning can enhance the clarity of your instructions and ensure viewers get the most out of your content. Balancing these can maximize both authenticity and educational value. Are there specific elements of your creative process you want to prioritize?\",\"Going with the flow might allow for more creativity and authenticity in your cooking videos. It can lead to spontaneous and engaging content that feels more personal and less constrained. If you enjoy expressing yourself freely, you might find this approach more fulfilling. Plus, it allows your unique personality to shine through, making your videos more relatable and enjoyable for viewers. Have you thought about which method resonates more with your natural style?\",\"Having a script might help streamline your cooking videos, making sure that you cover necessary details and keep the content organized. It could also help in reducing the anxiety of remembering what to say, allowing you to focus more on presenting and engaging with the audience. Have you weighed the benefits of structured preparation against the natural flow you're considering?\",\"Scripting your cooking videos can provide structure and ensure that you cover all the essential points you want to communicate. It could make the editing process smoother and help maintain a consistent flow in your videos. Plus, having a script might help you to stay focused on the educational aspect of your content, ensuring viewers take away clear, useful information. Have you considered how much time you want to dedicate to preparation versus filming?\"],\"terminal_expression\":{\"op\":\"var\",\"id\":\"response\"},\"personal_response_selection\":true,\"phase\":\"response_selection\",\"terminal_repair\":{\"expected_value\":\"Going with the flow might allow for more creativity and authenticity in your cooking videos. It can lead to spontaneous and engaging content that feels more personal and less constrained. If you enjoy expressing yourself freely, you might find this approach more fulfilling. Plus, it allows your unique personality to shine through, making your videos more relatable and enjoyable for viewers. Have you thought about which method resonates more with your natural style?\",\"feedback\":\"semantic_answer must equal the supported terminal value exactly, preserving its JSON type\",\"previous_semantic_answer\":null,\"previous_prediction\":null},\"source_documents\":{\"d1\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:a44ca93f001b14f6deabf95915b96c89c456b33307f339d168dbc79bb582865b\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":53.0,\"observed_end\":54.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d2\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:145c31806a41a34ea6d17afb883cfb2fb3fb61be4432f586e5cbd1d0f9251690\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":40.0,\"observed_end\":41.0,\"event_start\":null,\"event_end\":null,\"validity\":\"unknown\",\"time_source\":\"message_index\"}},\"d3\":{\"doc_id\":\"personamem:memory:f62437d2b5820b60e98e323c1f0c71ca06601dba246a55a821cb967eadaa7c58\",\"time_metadata\":{\"observed_start\":32.0,\"observed_end\":33.0,\"event_start\":nu